SWEET WLAN run G1 (patch 0167, boot-arg sweetwlan=11; consumes docs/research/83 (spec + rw_index_sz answer), 53 s1.5/s3, 71 (G1), run F3 wlan-runF3-0136; amended 2026-10-28 by docs/research/94 s.2 steps 3 and 8 + s.3 (golden ring depths, host trap page), SPEC-WIFI D-7/D-8).
Why: the msgbuf rings, the DMA index arrays and the scratch buffer live in host memory the dongle DMAs to; G2 (Command := 0x0406, ring_mem/host_cap writes, doorbell) needs their physical addresses and sizes, and the allocation must be proven before any bus write depends on it.
What: sweet_wlan_dma.h (pure, host test shim/wlan_dma_host_test.c, mutants tools/test_wlan_dma_mutants.py): swd_plan_make() lays out ONE block (5 rings 128x40, 2048x32, 64x24, 2048x24, 1024x40 = the Android golden depths [R94 s.2 step 8], 162304 B; scratch 8; 4 index arrays, rw_index_sz 4 x 43/43/4/4,
every buffer padded to 128 B; plus one 4 KiB zeroed host trap page [R94 step 3: host_trap_addr] at the next 4 KiB offset, total 167936 B; W-D4b D-10 amendment 2026-10-29: plus one 8192 B event buffer at the next 4 KiB offset, total 176128 B), swd_contig(), swd_audit_all(), swd_audit() = dhd_dma_buf_audit (pa != 0, aligned, 32-bit end does not wrap) + len multiple of 128. Glue sweet_wlan_g1() in sweet_wlan.c, level 11 = level 10 (run F3) unchanged + G1:
kmem_alloc_contig (patch 0028 precedent) page aligned (16K pages here: 176128 B -> 180224 allocated), zeroed; first and last page PAs must be contiguous (swd_contig); block and each sub-buffer audited (swd_audit_all); flush_dcache64 after the zeroing; prints "SWEET WLAN: G1 <name> pa=0x.. len=N" per buffer and "G1 done".
W-D4d amendment 2026-10-31 (sweetwlan>=17, used by patch 0174): plus one 8192 B ioctl-response buffer and one 8200 B ioctl payload buffer (padded to 8320 B), each at the next 4 KiB offset (176128 and 184320), total 192640 B -> 196608 allocated (12 pages); sizes from dhd_msgbuf.c:149 and :122-123; the block is 16 KiB larger at every sweetwlan>=11, no store changes.
W-D4e amendment 2026-10-31 (sweetwlan>=21, used by patch 0174; docs/research/W-D4e-scan24-design.md s.1 item 6): the event buffer and the ioctl-response buffer become 8 contiguous buffers of 8192 B each (65536 B each; DHD posts 8 response buffers, dhd_msgbuf.c:153), the payload buffer moves to 299008, total 307328 B (19 pages of 16 KiB). The plan is the same for every sweetwlan level.
Every failure has a swl_gap() on the line before its refusing printf (rule 8). The inputs rw_index_sz 4 / 43 / 4 are pinned from run F3 and a low gap says so (G2 re-reads them from the dongle).
NO bus access: HW-WRITE path none; the only memory touched is a fresh kernel allocation.

